# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/placeholders.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event capital_library_quiet_hour
# en: The Reading Room
title [379fa3] = 阅览室
# en: Upstairs from the archives, the Royal Library keeps a reading room for anyone who can whisper. The lamps are green, the chairs are hard and a librarian watches the door like a cat at a mousehole.
text [36014a] = 皇家图书馆的书库楼上，有一间阅览室，谁只要会压低声音都能进来。灯是绿的，椅子是硬的，一位图书管理员盯着门口，像猫守着老鼠洞。
# en: A vast reading room under a glass dome, green lamps on long tables, a few readers bent over their books in the hush.
scene [dc629b] = 玻璃穹顶下宽敞的阅览室，长桌上亮着绿色台灯，几位读者在静谧中埋头看书。
# en: Read a while
opt.left.label [f39033] = 读一会儿书
# en: {~An hour with a book you couldn't get at Lumenhold. Your neck aches; your head is full.|You read until the librarian's look becomes a cough. It was worth it.}
opt.left.say.1 [2694dc] = {~一个钟头，读了一本在流明霍尔德借不到的书。脖子酸了，脑子满了。|你一直读到图书管理员的眼神变成一声咳嗽。值了。}
# en: Just look at the dome
opt.right.label [359107] = 只看看穹顶
# en: {~You stand under the dome until your neck aches, then go out into the noise again.|Light falls through the glass in long dusty bars. You leave without reading a word.}
opt.right.say.1 [830ac3] = {~你站在穹顶下一直看到脖子发酸，然后回到外面的喧闹里。|光透过玻璃落成一道道带着灰尘的长条。你一个字也没读就走了。}

@event capital_townhouse_quiet_hour
# en: The Front Steps
title [caee80] = 门前台阶
# en: The townhouse is quiet this afternoon: the family is out calling, the cook is at the market and the steps have just been scrubbed. You could sit on them, if anyone sat on steps uptown.
text [5d369a] = 今天下午宅子里很安静：家里人出门拜客，厨子去了集市，台阶刚刚刷洗过。你可以坐在上面——如果上城有人坐台阶的话。
# en: Polished front steps of a tall uptown townhouse, a brass knocker shaped like a crest, the street busy with carriages below.
scene [b5bbef] = 上城一座高大宅邸前擦得锃亮的台阶，门环是一枚家徽的形状，下面的街上马车来来往往。
# en: Sit on the steps anyway
opt.left.label [6ee811] = 照样坐下
# en: {~You sit. Two carriages slow down to look. You wave. They don't.|The step is warm in the sun. A neighbour's footman pretends not to see you, very loudly.}
opt.left.say.1 [6b8c8c] = {~你坐下了。两辆马车放慢速度来看你。你挥手。他们没有。|台阶被太阳晒得暖暖的。邻居家的男仆假装没看见你，假装得非常大声。}
# en: Go in and rest
opt.right.label [c8b03f] = 进屋歇会儿
# en: {~Your old room, a cool sheet, the clock in the hall. You sleep an hour you didn't plan.|The house is so quiet you can hear the clock two floors down. You rest, and nobody asks you anything.}
opt.right.say.1 [8f4ef2] = {~你的老房间、一条凉凉的床单、门厅里的钟。你睡了一个计划外的钟头。|宅子静得能听见两层楼下的钟声。你歇着，没有人问你任何事。}

@event capital_club_quiet_hour
# en: The Porter's Look
title [b3c649] = 门房的眼神
# en: The members' club has a porter whose whole job is to decide who you are. He looks at your boots, then at your face, then at your boots again. "Members only, unless you're expected."
text [5a769d] = 会员俱乐部有一位门房，他全部的工作就是决定你是谁。他看看你的靴子，再看看你的脸，又看看你的靴子。“会员专用，除非有人在等你。”
# en: A dim club entrance of dark wood and brass, a porter in a waistcoat at a high desk looking a student up and down.
scene [a81bf8] = 一个深色木头和黄铜装饰的俱乐部门口，一位穿马甲的门房坐在高台后，上下打量着一个学生。
# en: Say you're expected
opt.left.label [f1d2ff] = 说有人在等你
# en: {~"By whom?" You name a patron off a portrait in the hall. He lets you as far as the cloakroom, which is more than most get.|He doesn't believe you, but he admires the attempt. You get a glass of water and a better story than you came in with.}
opt.left.say.1 [6486af] = {~“谁？”你随口报出门厅里一幅肖像画上赞助人的名字。他放你走到了衣帽间，这已经比大多数人走得远了。|他不信你，但欣赏你的胆量。你得到一杯水，还有一个比来时更好的故事。}
# en: Thank him and go
opt.right.label [b81b92] = 谢过他离开
# en: {~"Another time," he says, which means never, said kindly.|You leave. Through the window, someone laughs in a chair that costs more than your year.}
opt.right.say.1 [e059b5] = {~“改天吧，”他说，意思是永远不会，只是说得很客气。|你走了。窗户里，有人坐在一把比你一年开销还贵的椅子上大笑。}

@event capital_bazaar_quiet_hour
# en: A Hundred Stalls
title [c1a6cb] = 上百个摊位
# en: The Grand Bazaar is one long noise under a glass roof: spice-sellers, map-dealers, a woman selling birds that sing in other languages. You could lose an afternoon here. You could lose a purse.
text [a75f58] = 大集市是玻璃屋顶下一长串的喧闹：卖香料的、卖地图的，还有一个女人卖会用别国语言唱歌的鸟。你可以在这里丢掉一个下午，也可以丢掉一只钱袋。
# en: A vast covered market, light falling through high windows onto stalls of spices, maps, brass and coloured glass, crowds moving between them.
scene [d50e2e] = 一座巨大的有顶市场，光从高窗洒在香料、地图、黄铜器和彩色玻璃的摊位上，人群在其间穿行。
# en: Wander and look
opt.left.label [1c88ac] = 随便逛逛
# en: {~You come out with a paper of sugared almonds and no idea where the afternoon went.|A map-seller lets you hold a chart of a coast nobody has sailed. You buy a pastry to recover.}
opt.left.say.1 [7b1bed] = {~你出来时手里拿着一包糖杏仁，完全不知道下午去哪儿了。|一个卖地图的让你捧着一张没人航行过的海岸图。你买了块点心压压惊。}
# en: Keep your hand on your purse
opt.right.label [f13bb7] = 捂紧钱袋
# en: {~You walk the length of it with a hand on your purse and see almost nothing. Your purse thanks you.|You watch a pickpocket work a whole aisle. Educational.}
opt.right.say.1 [b8ce04] = {~你一手按着钱袋走完了全程，几乎什么都没看见。你的钱袋很感激。|你看着一个扒手把整条过道做了一遍。很有教育意义。}

@event capital_arcade_quiet_hour
# en: Brass Plates
title [7c7fef] = 铜牌
# en: The arcade sells everything that isn't a thing: a physician, a tutor, a scribe, a bathhouse, a portraitist and a fortune-teller who is, her plate says, "by appointment, mostly". Today you only read the plates.
text [bbc5f5] = 这条拱廊卖的全是不算东西的东西：一位医师、一位家庭教师、一位抄写员、一间浴场、一位肖像画师，还有一位算命人，她的牌子上写着“需预约，大多数时候”。今天你只是读读这些牌子。
# en: A long stone colonnade of open doors and polished brass nameplates, a bathhouse's steam drifting out of one archway.
scene [0a2e3b] = 一条长长的石砌柱廊，一扇扇开着的门和擦亮的铜名牌，一间浴场的蒸汽从一道拱门里飘出来。
# en: Steam at the bathhouse
opt.left.label [a72b8c] = 去浴场蒸一蒸
# en: {~The bathhouse is hot, tiled and full of retired admirals. You come out new.|Steam, cold plunge, steam again. Your shoulders forget the term.}
opt.left.say.1 [b3e8e9] = {~浴场又热又满是瓷砖，里面全是退休的海军将领。你出来时焕然一新。|蒸汽、冷水池、再来蒸汽。你的肩膀忘了这个学期。}
# en: Read the plates and walk on
opt.right.label [7e8ca4] = 读完牌子走开
# en: {~"Teeth drawn, letters written, futures read." You admire the ambition and walk on.|You read every plate twice. One just says "No."}
opt.right.say.1 [b82790] = {~“拔牙、代笔、看相。”你佩服这份雄心，继续往前走。|每块牌子你都读了两遍。有一块上面只写着“不”。}

@event capital_theatre_quiet_hour
# en: Gilt and Draughts
title [0f6392] = 金漆与穿堂风
# en: The theatre is between shows: chandeliers half-lit, the foyer smelling of dust and oranges. A stagehand on a ladder is pasting up a new playbill and getting most of the paste on himself.
text [4f2c05] = 剧院正处在两场演出之间：吊灯半亮，门厅里一股灰尘和橙子的气味。梯子上的场工在贴一张新戏单，大半浆糊都抹到了自己身上。
# en: The foyer of a grand gilded theatre, chandeliers half-lit, a playbill being pasted on a pillar by a stagehand on a ladder.
scene [97b94d] = 一座金碧辉煌的大剧院门厅，吊灯半亮着，一个场工站在梯子上往柱子上贴戏单。
# en: Hold his ladder
opt.left.label [56271c] = 帮他扶梯子
# en: {~He gives you a ticket for the gods in thanks. The gods are very high and very cheap and you love them.|You hold the ladder; he tells you which actress hates which. It's better than the play.}
opt.left.say.1 [b65060] = {~他送你一张顶层楼座的票作为谢礼。顶层楼座又高又便宜，你爱死了。|你扶着梯子，他告诉你哪位女演员讨厌哪位。比戏还好看。}
# en: Read the playbill
opt.right.label [83cd9d] = 读读戏单
# en: {~You learn the names off by heart, in case anyone asks. Nobody does, but you're ready.|A tragedy, a farce and a farce pretending to be a tragedy. You'd see all three.}
opt.right.say.1 [ca0a08] = {~你把名字全背了下来，以防有人问起。没人问，但你准备好了。|一出悲剧、一出闹剧，还有一出假装成悲剧的闹剧。三出你都想看。}

@event capital_guild_quiet_hour
# en: The Hiring Hall
title [a63480] = 招工棚
# en: The Guild works' hiring hall is a bench, a chalkboard and a foreman who looks at hands, not faces. Today the board says "NOTHING" in large letters, and under it, in smaller ones, "try tomorrow".
text [425111] = 公会工坊的招工棚只有一条长凳、一块黑板和一个只看手不看脸的工头。今天黑板上大大地写着“没有”，下面小字写着“明天再来”。
# en: A bare hiring hall at the gate of a great riverside works, a chalkboard of jobs, chimneys smoking beyond the window.
scene [afe190] = 河边大工坊门口一间光秃秃的招工棚，一块写着活计的黑板，窗外烟囱冒着烟。
# en: Wait in case
opt.left.label [470f79] = 等等看
# en: {~Nothing comes up, but the old hands on the bench argue about distillation for an hour and you listen to every word.|You wait. You learn three words for a burst vat, none polite.}
opt.left.say.1 [d1b621] = {~什么活也没来，但长凳上的老工人为蒸馏争了一个钟头，你一个字都没漏。|你等着。你学会了三种说大缸炸了的说法，没一种文雅。}
# en: Come back another day
opt.right.label [657555] = 改天再来
# en: {~"Tomorrow," the foreman says, which is what he says.|You leave the bench to the regulars.}
opt.right.say.1 [c65c61] = {~“明天，”工头说，他一向这么说。|你把长凳留给了常客们。}

@event capital_docks_quiet_hour
# en: Gulls and Cranes
title [732bcb] = 海鸥与吊车
# en: Port Calder's docks never stop: cranes, barrels, a ship from somewhere hot unloading something that smells of oranges. A boy offers to mind your bag for a penny, which is how bags go missing.
text [1ccfb3] = 考尔德港的码头从不停歇：吊车、木桶，一艘从某个炎热地方来的船正在卸一批闻起来像橙子的货。一个男孩提出帮你看包，收一个便士——包就是这么丢的。
# en: Busy harbour wharves at the river's mouth, cranes swinging crates off a tall ship, gulls wheeling over stacked barrels.
scene [2791d1] = 河口繁忙的港口码头，吊车从一艘高大的船上吊起箱子，海鸥在成堆的木桶上盘旋。
# en: Pay the boy
opt.left.label [8a2024] = 付钱给男孩
# en: {~He minds it beautifully and tells you which ships are smuggling. All of them, apparently.|Your bag comes back with everything in it and one extra orange. Business is business.}
opt.left.say.1 [14a642] = {~他把包看得好好的，还告诉你哪些船在走私。据他说，全部都是。|你的包回来时东西一样不少，还多了一个橙子。生意就是生意。}
# en: Keep your bag
opt.right.label [fa77f5] = 自己看着包
# en: {~You keep your bag and watch the boy offer the same deal to a sailor, who laughs and pays. You learn something.|"Suit yourself." He's gone before you see him go.}
opt.right.say.1 [c4caf2] = {~你没让他看包，却看着他向一个水手开出同样的价，水手笑着付了钱。你学到了点东西。|“随你。”你还没看清他走，他就没影了。}

@event capital_counting_house_quiet_hour
# en: The Ledgers Below
title [8e0c53] = 楼下的账簿
# en: Below, the clerks are at their ledgers; above, your old room. The old clerk at the end desk has been here longer than the door, and looks at you as if you're a column that doesn't add up.
text [418bcc] = 楼下，账房们伏在账簿上；楼上，是你的老房间。尽头那张桌子边的老账房在这儿待得比那扇门还久，他看你的眼神，像在看一列加不平的数。
# en: A counting house on a wharf, high desks and tall ledgers below, a staircase rising to living rooms above, a clerk with an ink-stained cuff.
scene [0b6e97] = 码头上的一座账房，楼下是高高的写字台和厚账簿，楼梯通往楼上的住处，一个账房的袖口沾着墨水。
# en: Help with a column
opt.left.label [9b7345] = 帮忙算一列账
# en: {~You find the error. He finds two more of yours. Honours even, and a coin for the trouble.|An hour of numbers. The old clerk says "Hm" at the end, which from him is a medal.}
opt.left.say.1 [4de811] = {~你找出了那个错。他找出了你的两个。打个平手，外加一枚辛苦钱。|一个钟头的数字。最后老账房说了声“嗯”，这在他那儿就是勋章了。}
# en: Go up and rest
opt.right.label [444519] = 上楼歇着
# en: {~Your old room still smells of ink. You sleep to the sound of the tide.|Upstairs, the noise of the wharf is a lullaby you'd forgotten.}
opt.right.say.1 [897ab0] = {~你的老房间还是一股墨水味。你伴着潮声睡着了。|在楼上，码头的嘈杂成了一首你忘了的摇篮曲。}

@event capital_crew_loft_quiet_hour
# en: The Old Stove
title [c7c990] = 老炉子
# en: The crew's loft is the same as ever: hammocks, a stove that smokes, a card game that has been going on since you left. "Look who it is," says someone, "the wizard."
text [15754c] = 伙伴们的阁楼还是老样子：吊床、一只冒烟的炉子，还有一局从你走后就没停过的牌。“瞧瞧谁来了，”有人说，“大巫师。”
# en: A loft above a chandler's shop, hammocks slung between beams, a pot-bellied stove, young people playing cards in its warmth.
scene [49833f] = 一家船具店楼上的阁楼，横梁间挂着吊床，一只大肚炉子，几个年轻人在炉边打牌。
# en: Sit in on the game
opt.left.label [cb3c92] = 坐下来打一局
# en: {~You lose two hands and win back one, and they all pretend you cheated. It's the best evening in months.|They deal you in like you never left. You lose, on purpose, mostly.}
opt.left.say.1 [de6e2e] = {~你输了两把、赢回一把，他们全都假装你出老千。这是几个月来最好的一个晚上。|他们给你发牌，好像你从没离开过。你输了，大多是故意的。}
# en: Sleep in your old hammock
opt.right.label [0a0d0f] = 睡你的老吊床
# en: {~The hammock still knows your shape. You sleep through the card game, the stove and an argument about a dog.|You sleep like you used to, with one hand on your boots.}
opt.right.say.1 [77373d] = {~吊床还记得你的形状。你一觉睡过了牌局、炉子，还有一场关于一条狗的争吵。|你像从前那样睡着，一只手按着靴子。}

@event countryside_mill_quiet_hour
# en: The Turning Wheel
title [8c905e] = 转动的水车
# en: The mill wheel turns slowly, the chapel stands small and grey, and on the green the children skip to a rhyme with a lot of counting in it. They stop when you come near, and smile, and start again when you've passed.
text [b8df5b] = 水车慢慢地转，礼拜堂又小又灰，绿地上孩子们唱着一首数数特别多的歌谣跳绳。你一走近，他们就停下来冲你笑；你走过去了，他们又开始。
# en: A mill on a slow river in a small grey village, its wheel turning, children skipping a rope on the green in front of the chapel.
scene [0501dc] = 一个灰色小村里慢慢河流上的一座磨坊，水车转动，孩子们在礼拜堂前的绿地上跳绳。
# en: Watch the wheel a while
opt.left.label [3cb04a] = 看一会儿水车
# en: {~The wheel goes round, the water goes over, and the afternoon goes with it.|You watch the wheel until you notice the river is lower than the wheel is fast. Probably nothing.}
opt.left.say.1 [9efdf6] = {~水车转着，水漫过去，下午也跟着过去了。|你看着水车，直到发觉河水比水车转得慢。大概没什么。}
# en: Walk on through
opt.right.label [75daa8] = 穿村而过
# en: {~The village waves you off. All of it.|You walk on. Behind you, the skipping starts again, counting.}
opt.right.say.1 [f4db9b] = {~整个村子都在送你。每一个人。|你继续往前走。身后，跳绳又开始了，还在数数。}

@event countryside_marsh_quiet_hour
# en: Lights on the Water
title [8bf099] = 水上的光
# en: The Marsh is reeds, black water and a path that's there until it isn't. At dusk, little lights come out and hang over the pools. A house on stilts stands at the edge with a lamp in its window.
text [1515d3] = 沼泽是芦苇、黑水，还有一条路——直到它不再是路。黄昏时，小小的光点出来，悬在水塘上方。沼泽边上一座高脚屋的窗里亮着一盏灯。
# en: Reed beds and black water at dusk, small pale lights hanging low over the marsh, a house on stilts at its edge.
scene [06c465] = 黄昏时的芦苇丛和黑水，几点苍白的光低低地悬在沼泽上，沼泽边上有一座高脚屋。
# en: Watch the lights from the path
opt.left.label [a6916a] = 从小路上看那些光
# en: {~The lights drift together and apart, as if they're talking. You don't follow them, which is the main thing.|One light comes nearer than the others. You keep to the path, and it goes away, disappointed.}
opt.left.say.1 [aa39c3] = {~光点聚了又散，像在交谈。你没去追，这才是要紧的。|有一个光点比别的靠得更近。你守在路上，它失望地走了。}
# en: Turn back before dark
opt.right.label [68600c] = 天黑前回去
# en: {~You turn back while the path is still a path.|You leave the Marsh to its lights.}
opt.right.say.1 [d23b31] = {~趁路还是路，你往回走了。|你把沼泽留给了它的光。}

@event countryside_moors_quiet_hour
# en: The Third Cairn
title [22174a] = 第三座石堆
# en: The moors go on longer than they should. A shepherd tells you to stay this side of the third cairn, then walks off before you can ask why. Fog is coming up in the hollows, unhurried.
text [3d415f] = 荒原比它应有的更长。一个牧羊人叫你别越过第三座石堆，你还没来得及问为什么，他就走开了。洼地里的雾正不慌不忙地升起来。
# en: Open moorland of heather and grey stone cairns, fog rising in the hollows, a lone sheep watching from a rock.
scene [ad2313] = 开阔的石南荒原，灰色的石堆，洼地里升起雾气，一只孤零零的羊站在岩石上看着。
# en: Walk to the first cairn and back
opt.left.label [416e51] = 走到第一座石堆再回来
# en: {~The wind is clean and enormous. You touch the cairn, count to ten, and come back with your cheeks burning.|You reach the first cairn. The second is closer than it looked. You turn back anyway.}
opt.left.say.1 [bfac39] = {~风干净又辽阔。你摸了摸石堆，数到十，回来时脸颊发烫。|你走到了第一座石堆。第二座比看上去近。你还是转身回来了。}
# en: Stay by the road
opt.right.label [569d44] = 待在路边
# en: {~You watch the fog fill the hollows from the road, which is the sensible place to watch it from.|A sheep stares at you until you leave. You leave.}
opt.right.say.1 [c17d36] = {~你在路边看着雾填满洼地，路边正是看雾的明智之处。|一只羊一直盯着你，直到你离开。你离开了。}

@event countryside_ridge_quiet_hour
# en: The Stones
title [fa1976] = 立石
# en: The stones on the ridge stand in a ring, leaning a little, as if listening to the valley. From up here you can see both villages, the fen and the moors, and the road joining them like a stitch.
text [246133] = 山脊上的立石围成一圈，微微倾斜，像在聆听山谷。从这里你能看见两个村子、沼泽和荒原，还有把它们连起来的那条路，像一道针脚。
# en: A ring of grey standing stones on a bare ridge under a huge sky, the valley's villages small and far below.
scene [80c369] = 光秃秃的山脊上，巨大的天空下一圈灰色立石，山谷里的村子又小又远。
# en: Count the stones
opt.left.label [910e63] = 数数这些石头
# en: {~You count them twice and get two answers. You decide it's the wind.|Nineteen, you think. Or twenty. You stop counting.}
opt.left.say.1 [5a4321] = {~你数了两遍，得到两个答案。你决定怪风。|十九块，你想。也许二十。你不数了。}
# en: Just take in the view
opt.right.label [b51fff] = 只看风景
# en: {~The whole valley, small and peaceful, from up here. It looks very well kept.|The wind tugs your coat and the villages smoke quietly below. Nothing up here wants anything from you.}
opt.right.say.1 [a8eee7] = {~从这里看，整个山谷又小又安宁，打理得非常好。|风拽着你的外套，村子在下面安静地冒着炊烟。这上面没有任何东西想从你身上要什么。}

@event travel_city_morning
# en: A Morning in the Capital
title [ec0430] = 王都的早晨
# en: The capital wakes before you do, and louder: barrows, bells, a man selling hot chestnuts under your window as if his life depends on it, which it may.
text [d84e63] = 王都比你醒得早，也更吵：手推车、钟声，还有一个在你窗下卖热栗子的人，卖得像性命攸关——也许真是。
# en: Early morning in a capital city, a student at a lodging-house window looking down at barrows, bells and smoke.
scene [10be04] = 王都的清晨，一个学生站在旅店窗前，俯瞰手推车、钟声和烟雾。
# en: Chestnuts for breakfast
opt.left.label [84fde4] = 栗子当早饭
# en: {~They burn your fingers and taste of smoke and autumn. A good start.|You eat them walking, like a native, and get lost like a visitor.}
opt.left.say.1 [b57e70] = {~烫手，带着烟和秋天的味道。好的开头。|你边走边吃，像个本地人；然后迷路，像个外地人。}
# en: Plan the day over cheap tea
opt.right.label [07927a] = 就着便宜茶安排一天
# en: {~You draw a map of the day on the back of a playbill. The capital ignores it completely.|Cheap tea, a borrowed newspaper, a plan. Good enough.}
opt.right.say.1 [1b55e6] = {~你在一张戏单背面画了一天的地图。王都完全不理它。|便宜的茶、一份借来的报纸、一个计划。够了。}

@event travel_country_morning
# en: A Morning in the Countryside
title [ecfd29] = 乡间的早晨
# en: The country wakes slowly: a cart in the lane, mist on the fields, a rooster with opinions. Your host has left bread and a jug of milk outside your door, and a sprig of something green tied round the jug.
text [9cd336] = 乡间醒得慢：小路上一辆马车、田野上的雾，还有一只很有主见的公鸡。房东在你门外放了面包和一罐牛奶，罐子上系着一小枝绿色的什么。
# en: Early morning in a country village, mist on the fields, a student at a window watching a farmer lead a cart down the lane.
scene [acf3f1] = 乡村的清晨，田野上有雾，一个学生在窗前看着农夫牵着马车走过小路。
# en: Breakfast at the window
opt.left.label [b7c388] = 在窗边吃早饭
# en: {~The bread is still warm. The mist lifts off the fields like a lid.|You eat slowly, watching the village wake. Everyone waves at your window.}
opt.left.say.1 [5cc4d5] = {~面包还是温的。雾像盖子一样从田野上揭开。|你慢慢吃着，看着村子醒来。每个人都朝你的窗户挥手。}
# en: Walk out early
opt.right.label [ce7383] = 一早出门走走
# en: {~You walk the lane before anyone is up. The fields are very quiet, and the scarecrows are very well dressed.|An early walk, wet boots, and the whole valley to yourself.}
opt.right.say.1 [bb405a] = {~趁大家还没起，你走了一趟小路。田野非常安静，稻草人穿得非常体面。|一早的散步、湿透的靴子，还有整个山谷只属于你。}
